<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23404" root="شوه" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاوِىٌّ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاهِىٌّ</span></b>  A man <i>possessing</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَآء</span> [meaning <i>sheep</i> or <i>goats</i> or <i>both</i>]: (K:) the former is
the rel. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَآءٌ</span>; and the latter, that of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاةٌ</span>: but
used as a proper name of a man, it is ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَائِىٌّ</span></b> , and,
if you will, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاوِىٌّ</span>. (S, TA. *)

